  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday Night through Monday)\nIssued at 950 PM CST Mon Nov 16 2026\n\nMild and breezy southerly flow will continue through the week \nwith gradually warming temperatures. High temperatures will reach \nthe low 70s by late week. Low level moisture will increase, with \ndew points rising into the 50s. The higher moisture levels will \nkeep fire weather potential on the lower side.\n\nBy late in the week, ensemble guidance is in good agreement that a \nchunk of the persistent trough along the west coast will eject \ninland through the Plains. This will send a cold front through the \narea along with at least a chance of rain and thunderstorms. With \nthat said, guidance is inconsistent on whether this will occur, \nshowing perhaps a 30-50% chance of rain for now, which is lower than \nwhat was shown yesterday for the same period. The bigger story will \nlikely be the cooler temperatures, which should fall down closer to \nseasonal norms. Additional rain chances will move into the area \nearly next week.",
